## React Component Lifecycle
Lifecycle means:
Different stages a component goes through from creation to removal.

Lifecycle Phases
Mounting
Updating
Unmounting

What are Lifecycle Events?
Lifecycle events are methods/functions executed during different stages of component life.
Event Definition
An event is an action or occurrence detected by the application.

Examples:

Mouse click
Keyboard press
Form submit
Component loading
Event Categories in React
Mouse Events
Keyboard Events
Form Events
Lifecycle Events

1. Mouse Events

Examples:

onClick
onMouseOver
Example
<button onClick={() => alert("Button Clicked")}>
    Click
</button>

2. Keyboard Events

Examples:

onKeyDown
onKeyUp
Example
<input onKeyDown={() => console.log("Key Pressed")} />

3. Form Events

Examples:

onSubmit
onChange
Example
<form onSubmit={() => alert("Form Submitted")}>

</form>

Mounting Phase
Mounting means:
Component is created and inserted into DOM.